\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The state is the whole tuple}
\date{2026-11-25}

\p{In \ref{fnip-0005} the state is the pair #{(V,n)}. The voltage
recording is the coordinate #{V} of that pair. A coordinate name is
part of the chosen tuple. A construction on the state uses that
point.}

\p{Izhikevich names one such point with 4 coordinates. The state of the
Hodgkin–Huxley model is the vector #{(V,m,n,h)\in\mathbb{R}^{4}}
\citet{p. 58}{izhikevich2007dynamical}. Section 2.3.1 writes a
differential equation for each of #{V}, #{n}, #{m} and #{h}, on
p. 37 of the same book. The pair in \ref{fnip-0005} is the planar
case of the same idea.}
